      <method name="set_accessible_parent" c:identifier="gtk_accessible_set_accessible_parent" version="4.10">
        <doc xml:space="preserve" filename="gtk/gtkaccessible.c" line="154">
          Sets the parent and sibling of an accessible object.

This function is meant to be used by accessible implementations that are
not part of the widget hierarchy, and but act as a logical bridge between
widgets. For instance, if a widget creates an object that holds metadata
for each child, and you want that object to implement the `GtkAccessible`
interface, you will use this function to ensure that the parent of each
child widget is the metadata object, and the parent of each metadata
object is the container widget.
        </doc>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <type name="none" c:type="void"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
            <type name="Accessible" c:type="GtkAccessible*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
          <parameter name="parent" transfer-ownership="none" nullable="1" allow-none="1">
            <type name="Accessible" c:type="GtkAccessible*"/>
          </parameter>
          <parameter name="next_sibling" transfer-ownership="none" nullable="1" allow-none="1">
            <type name="Accessible" c:type="GtkAccessible*"/>
          </parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
      <method name="update_next_accessible_sibling" c:identifier="gtk_accessible_update_next_accessible_sibling" version="4.10">
        <doc xml:space="preserve" filename="gtk/gtkaccessible.c" line="192">
          Updates the next accessible sibling.

That might be useful when a new child of a custom accessible
is created, and it needs to be linked to a previous child.
        </doc>
